{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791641185,"nonce":"U8VJrxV1WQXAtupG0OAPZ8Iqtus=","title":"cn accordion and collapsible rebuild to open and shut, because height could only change by rebuilding","message":"Both decided a section's open or shut height when the element was built: shut was `.when(!open, |d| d.h(0.0))`, so changing it meant rebuilding. The accordion was one Stateful over every section (deps on all their open states), so opening one rebuilt them all and their content; the collapsible's body was a Stateful on its open state, and its trigger a Stateful\u003cButtonState\u003e for hover and the chevron. The FLIP height animation (`animate_bounds`) ran off the rebuilt bounds.\n\nThe visual-animation pass compares a keyed node's laid-out bounds with what was last drawn after every layout pass, not only after a rebuild, so a height changed in place animates the same way.\n\nFix:\n\n- `Div::collapsed_when(condition)`: height 0 while the condition holds, auto otherwise, through a layout binding like `absolute_when`. The content stays laid out and painted; with `overflow_clip` it is cut off, so a height animation shows it closing. min-height needs no handling: CSS (and taffy) cap an item's content-based minimum at its specified size, so `height: 0` gives a minimum of 0, which is what the old `.h(0.0)` relied on.\n- accordion: built once; each section's content is `collapsed_when` a computed over its open state, its padding moved to an inner wrapper so a shut section has none; the chevron turns by a bound rotation.\n- collapsible: the body is built once with `collapsed_when`; the trigger is a plain Div with its fill a computed over an Interaction and a bound chevron rotation. Its ElementBuilder impl now forwards event_handlers and element_id, which a Div needs and the Stateful did not.\n- cn tests' common: a reference to the shared scheduler and `tick_animations(dt)`, so a test can step animations.\n\nTests: `blinc_layout/tests/collapsed_when.rs` (state, computed, constant); `blinc_cn/tests/accordion_in_place.rs` (opens in place and the chevron turns; the drawn height on the first frame is between 0 and full and settles at full; single mode closes the other section); `blinc_cn/tests/collapsible_in_place.rs` (the section follows its state set from anywhere; the trigger's chevron turns and fill follows hover). All accordion and collapsible tests fail against the old components.","files":null}]}